A person must not be registered to manage the funding of supports under participants’ plans unless a deed of arrangement that meets the requirements in subsection (2) is in force between the person and the Agency.
A deed of arrangement must include the following:
(a) standards and processes to be met by the person in relation to integrity and governance, including reporting requirements to the Agency;
(b) standards to be met by the person in relation to staff, including requirements to be satisfied in relation to key personnel of the person;
(c) requirements to be met by the person for the handling and submitting of claims to the Agency, including verification of identity and verification of the provision of supports;
(d) standards and requirements to be met by the person in relation to information and communications technology and systems;
(e) requirements to be met by the person and key personnel of the person in relation to related parties and managing and divesting conflicts of interest.
(2A) A person is a related party of another person in any of the following circumstances:
(a) the person is a relative of the other person (within the meaning of section 9 of the Corporations Act 2001 );
(b) either person is an associated entity of the other person (within the meaning of section 50AAA of the Corporations Act 2001 );
(c) circumstances prescribed by the National Disability Insurance Scheme Rules for the purposes of this paragraph.
The Agency must keep a public register of registered plan management providers.

